t/actions/runs/37473604910/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/actions/runs/37473604910/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/actions/workflows/340629606","head_commit":{"id":"17eca7b0263abbe4aeaa2f5b149c5071b0890f06","tree_id":"9f402fa7bd561d3518df76bb68e22f96235f85aa","message":"[Flight] Fix reviving errors without stack frames in debug info (#37730)\n\n## Summary\n\n`serializeDebugErrorValue` outlines the error info with `objectLimit:\nstack.length * 2 + 1`, but the error info object itself uses one from\nthat budget. With zero frames the limit is 1, so the empty `stack` array\ngets deferred and goes out as `\"$Y\"`. The client then gets a string\nplaceholder where it expects an array, `buildFakeCallStack` throws on\nit, and the error fails to revive. For an `AggregateError` that failure\nleaves `errors` as `null`, so `AggregateError(null, ...)` throws during\nparsing and the root never resolves.\n\nErrors from Node internals (like the `ECONNREFUSED` from happy eyeballs\nin the issue) have no frames, so they hit this when they show up as a\nrejected I/O value or in a replayed log. Bumping the limit by one leaves\nroom for the stack array itself.","timestamp":"2026-10-06T13:42:47Z","author":{"name":"Lazizbek Ergashev","email":"lazerg2@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com"}},"repository":{"id":10270250,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxMDI3MDI1MA==","name":"react","full_name":"react/react","private":false,"owner":{"login":"react","id":102812,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEwMjgxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102812?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/react","html_url":"https://github.com/react","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/react/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/react/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/react/gists{/gist_id}","starred_ur